scripts/check-generated-tree-freshness.mjs is the one staleness predicate for the committed generated trees — modified, untracked, and deleted paths all count — and validate.sh's freshness block and the release workflow's guard steps both invoke that script rather than hand-rolled git checks; a caller that measures with its own git predicate reintroduces the local-green/CI-red divergence the predicate exists to prevent, and its failure text branches on the build driver's exit-code contract so each reachable cause reads differently.
